<%# Effect list in the closed primitive vocabulary (§3.1). Params a primitive doesn't take are ignored. %>
<fieldset class="panel">
  <legend>Effects</legend>
  <p class="hint">Applied in order to each target. Leave a row's primitive blank to remove it. Cleanse cures the status picked, or every harmful one when none is. Away takes "who" off the field for its duration; with power, they come back striking. Sap takes MP and the user keeps "Keep %" of it. Damage can do "Bonus %" (×2 when blank) against a status, a type, the undead or bosses; "Recoil %" of it hurts the user; "Grudge %" more power comes as the user nears the end of their HP. A Doom status knocks its target out when it runs out. Summon calls a creature from the Bestiary to the user's side: it acts at once and stays for its duration, or, at duration 0, while its summoner stands (down, it takes them with it), or the whole battle with Stays. Gather puts stacks of a stacking status on the user (Amount, 1 when blank); a blow "With" that status gets "Boost %" more power for each stack and spends them, unless it holds them. "Patience %" more power comes for everyone who went before the user that round. "Pierce %" of the target's defence counts for nothing; Unresisted treats a resistance as neutral. "Triage %" more healing comes the lower the target. Steal with Boon takes one of the target's good statuses. Transform puts on a mask from the Armory. Grab holds the target fast for its duration: a blow on the user from the target's side breaks it ("Breaks": any blow, or only one of a type), and it then loses "Tear %" of its HP; the user falling or leaving lets go. A blow with "Stumble" that misses leaves the user down for those turns. An away that's Aloft is up out of reach of blows, but spells still find it.</p>
  <table class="grid-form" data-controller="rows">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Primitive</th><th>Power</th><th>Hits</th><% if types_matter? %><th>Type</th><% end %><th>Status</th><th>Chance %</th>
        <th>Duration</th><th>Stat</th><th>Amount %</th><th>Revive %</th><th>Who</th><th>Keep %</th><th>Against</th><th>Bonus %</th><th>Recoil %</th><th>Grudge %</th><th>Creature</th>
        <th>Pierce %</th><th>Unresisted</th><th>With</th><th>Boost %</th><th>Hold</th><th>Patience %</th><th>Triage %</th><th>Boon</th><th>Stays</th><th>Mask</th><th>Breaks</th><th>Tear %</th><th>Stumble</th><th>Aloft</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody data-rows-target="body">
      <% rows_with_blanks(f.object.effects).each_with_index do |effect, i| %>
        <% name = ->(key) { json_field_name(f, :effects, i, key) } %>
        <tr>
          <td><%= select_tag name.(:primitive), options_for_select(Battle::PRIMITIVES.map { |p| [term(p), p] }, effect["primitive"]), include_blank: true, "aria-label": "Primitive #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:power), effect["power"], min: 1, "aria-label": "Power #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:hits), effect["hits"], min: 1, "aria-label": "Hits #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <% if types_matter? %>
            <td><%= select_tag name.(:type), options_for_select(type_options, effect["type"]), include_blank: true, "aria-label": "Type #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <% elsif effect["type"] %>
            <%= hidden_field_tag name.(:type), effect["type"], id: nil %>
          <% end %>
          <%# The statuses a Status effect can give: those with a primitive of their own (charging, shield…) come from it. %>
          <td><%= select_tag name.(:kind), options_for_select((Battle::STATUSES - Battle::PRIMITIVE_STATUSES).map { |s| [term(s), s] }, effect["kind"]), include_blank: true, "aria-label": "Status #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:chance), effect["chance"], min: 0, max: 100, "aria-label": "Chance #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:duration), effect["duration"], min: 0, "aria-label": "Duration #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= select_tag name.(:stat), options_for_select(Stats::MODIFIABLE.map { |s| [stat_label(s), s] }, effect["stat"]), include_blank: true, "aria-label": "Stat #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:amount), effect["amount"], "aria-label": "Amount #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:fraction), effect["fraction"], min: 0, max: 100, "aria-label": "Revive fraction #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= select_tag name.(:who), options_for_select([ [ "The user", "self" ], [ "The target", "target" ] ], effect["who"]), include_blank: true, "aria-label": "Who goes, #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:keep), effect["keep"], min: 0, max: 100, "aria-label": "MP kept, #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td>
            <%= select_tag name.(:against), grouped_options_for_select({ "Traits" => Battle::AGAINST_TRAITS.map { |t| [ t.capitalize, t ] },
                                                                      "Statuses" => Battle::STATUSES.map { |st| [ term(st), st ] },
                                                                      "Types" => (types_matter? ? type_options : []) }, effect["against"]),
                           include_blank: true, "aria-label": "Bonus against, #{i + 1}" %>
          </td>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:bonus), effect["bonus"], min: 0, max: Battle::MAX_BONUS, placeholder: 200, "aria-label": "Bonus, #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:recoil), effect["recoil"], min: 0, max: 100, "aria-label": "Recoil, #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:grudge), effect["grudge"], min: 0, max: Battle::MAX_BONUS, "aria-label": "Grudge, #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= select_tag name.(:creature), options_for_select(@world.monsters.order(:name).map { |m| [ m.name, m.slug ] }, effect["creature"]), include_blank: true, "aria-label": "Creature, #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <% flag = ->(key, label) { select_tag(name.(key), options_for_select([ [ "Yes", 1 ] ], effect[key.to_s]), include_blank: true, "aria-label": "#{label}, #{i + 1}") } %>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:pierce), effect["pierce"], min: 0, max: 100, "aria-label": "Pierce, #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= flag.(:unresisted, "Unresisted") %></td>
          <td><%= select_tag name.(:with), options_for_select(Battle::STATUSES.map { |st| [ term(st), st ] }, effect["with"]), include_blank: true, "aria-label": "With a status on the user, #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:boost), effect["boost"], min: 0, max: Battle::MAX_BONUS, placeholder: 50, "aria-label": "Boost, #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= flag.(:hold, "Hold") %></td>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:patience), effect["patience"], min: 0, max: Battle::MAX_BONUS, "aria-label": "Patience, #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:triage), effect["triage"], min: 0, max: Battle::MAX_BONUS, "aria-label": "Triage, #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= flag.(:boon, "Steal a status") %></td>
          <td><%= flag.(:stays, "Stays the battle") %></td>
          <td><%= select_tag name.(:mask), options_for_select(@world.items.masks.order(:name).map { |m| [ m.name, m.slug ] }, effect["mask"]), include_blank: true, "aria-label": "Mask, #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= select_tag name.(:breaks), options_for_select([ [ "Any blow", "hit" ] ] + (types_matter? ? type_options : []), effect["breaks"]), include_blank: true, "aria-label": "Breaks the grab, #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:tear), effect["tear"], min: 0, max: 100, "aria-label": "Tear, #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= number_field_tag name.(:stumble), effect["stumble"], min: 1, max: Battle::MAX_STUMBLE, "aria-label": "Stumble, #{i + 1}" %></td>
          <td><%= flag.(:aloft, "Aloft") %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
    <tfoot><tr><td colspan="99"><button type="button" class="button button--quiet" data-action="rows#add">Add a row</button></td></tr></tfoot>
  </table>
</fieldset>
